  ],
  "nameOrigin": "From the Greek chroma, 'colour', for its brightly coloured compounds.",
  "source": "pubchem",
  "note": "Found in crocoite, the 'Siberian red lead' mineral; Vauquelin obtained the metal the following year by heating the oxide with charcoal.",
